---
layout: layouts/base.njk
title: "Yelp topical authority map"
description: "Internal tool. The Yelp content plan against what the build actually produced."
permalink: /yelp-map/index.html

# NOINDEX, WAY ONE OF FOUR. Read by base.njk, which ORs it with the deploy
# rule, so this page carries the directive on production too, where every other
# page carries none.
noindex: true

# NOINDEX, WAY TWO. Out of collections.all, which is the set any sitemap
# iterates. There is no sitemap.xml in this repo yet; this is what keeps the
# page out of the one that gets written, with no edit to it and nobody having
# to remember. Same key robots.njk uses, for the same reason.
eleventyExcludeFromCollections: true
---
{% from "components/container.njk" import container %}

{#
  THE YELP MAP, at /yelp-map/. INTERNAL TOOL. Not for publication.

  ============================================================
  DERIVE, DO NOT TRUST. That is the whole design.
  ============================================================

  src/_data/yelpMap.js is a hand-maintained plan and it says so about itself:
  several rows are marked source: "plan", meaning asserted and not confirmed,
  and the file records that the plan has been wrong at least once. So for any
  entry whose url matches a page the build produced, the build wins and the
  file's state is not consulted. See the yelpMapReport filter, where all of it
  is computed; this template only renders.

  THE ONE DISTINCTION THIS PAGE EXISTS TO SHOW is publishable against not.
  A page with zero brackets and zero placeholder slots can go out. A page with
  either renders, looks finished, and passes all five checks in verify, and must
  not. Nothing else on the site draws that line and it is invisible from a URL.

  WHERE THE FILE AND THE BUILD DISAGREE, BOTH ARE SHOWN. Nothing here resolves
  one into the other: a row that claims SHIPPED with no page behind it is either
  a wrong plan or an incomplete build, and those have different fixes.

  NO NEW COMPONENTS AND NO NEW TOKENS. Everything below is .cs-eyebrow, the type
  scale and the colour tokens that already exist. The page-scoped rules in
  yelp-map.css are layout only.

  FOUR-WAY NOINDEX, and the two that are not in the front matter above:
  robots.njk Disallows /yelp-map/ on every deploy, and nothing anywhere links
  here. The nav is in src/_data/nav.js and the footer reads the same file; this
  URL is in neither, and being out of collections.all means no future listing
  can pick it up either.
#}

{#- THE templateContent READ IS HERE, IN THE TEMPLATE, AND NOT IN THE FILTER.

    That is not a style choice. Eleventy only defers a page until the pages it
    measures have rendered when it sees `templateContent` read in the template's
    own source; the same read inside a filter is invisible to its dependency
    graph, and the build fails with TemplateContentPrematureUseError on the
    first article it reaches. Measured: identical filter, one line moved, exit 1
    to exit 0.

    So the template gathers rendered bodies and the filter measures them. The
    filter never touches templateContent, which also means it can be handed any
    list of {url, html} and stays testable. -#}
{%- set rendered = [] %}
{%- for article in collections.yelpArticles %}
  {%- set rendered = (rendered.push({
        url: article.url,
        inputPath: article.inputPath,
        html: article.templateContent
      }), rendered) %}
{%- endfor %}

{%- set report = yelpMap | yelpMapReport(rendered, collections.builtUrls) %}

{% call container(class="cs-map-page") %}

  <header class="cs-map-head">
    <p class="cs-eyebrow">Internal tool, not for publication</p>
    <h1 class="cs-map-h1">Yelp topical authority map</h1>
    <p class="cs-map-lede">
      The content plan in <code>src/_data/yelpMap.js</code> against what the build
      actually produced. Where a URL matches a built page, every number on this
      row is measured off the rendered article and the file's own state is
      ignored.
    </p>

    <dl class="cs-map-totals">
      <div><dt>Clusters</dt><dd>{{ report.totals.clusters }}</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Spokes</dt><dd>{{ report.totals.spokes }}</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Page templates</dt><dd>{{ report.totals.templates }}</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Built</dt><dd>{{ report.totals.built }}</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Publishable</dt><dd>{{ report.totals.publishable }}</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Dev only</dt><dd class="cs-map-flag">{{ report.totals.onDevOnly }}</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Migration</dt><dd>{{ report.totals.migration }}</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Disagreements</dt><dd class="cs-map-flag">{{ report.totals.disagreements }}</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Blockers</dt><dd class="cs-map-flag">{{ report.totals.blockers }}</dd></div>
      <div><dt>FAQs</dt><dd>{{ report.faqs.total }}, {{ report.faqs.linkableToday }} linkable</dd></div>
    </dl>
  </header>

  {#- ---- ONE ROW, USED BY EVERY SECTION ----

      A macro rather than the same twenty lines three times. It renders what is
      KNOWN about an entry, which means the derived half when there is one and
      the file's half when there is not, and it never merges the two. -#}
  {%- macro row(entry, kind) %}
  <div class="cs-map-row{{ " cs-map-row--flag" if entry.disagreement or (entry.derived and not entry.derived.publishable) }}">
    <p class="cs-map-row__head">
      {#- STATE. Derived where the build knows, and labelled as derived, so a
          reader can tell a measurement from an assertion at a glance. -#}
      {%- if entry.derived %}
      <span class="cs-map-state{{ " cs-map-state--ok" if entry.derived.publishable else " cs-map-state--dev" }}">
        {{- "Shipped" if entry.derived.publishable else "Dev only" -}}
      </span>
      <span class="cs-map-src">measured</span>
      {%- elif entry.builtNotArticle %}
      {#- The page exists and is not an article, so there is nothing to count.
          Said out loud: an empty counts row would read as zero words. -#}
      <span class="cs-map-state cs-map-state--ok">Built</span>
      <span class="cs-map-src">page template, not measured</span>
      {%- else %}
      <span class="cs-map-state cs-map-state--plan">{{ entry.state }}</span>
      <span class="cs-map-src">{{ entry.source }}</span>
      {%- endif %}

      {%- if entry.derived or entry.builtNotArticle %}
      <a class="cs-map-row__title" href="{{ entry.url }}">{{ entry.title }}</a>
      {%- else %}
      <span class="cs-map-row__title">{{ entry.title }}</span>
      {%- endif %}

      {#- MIGRATION IS MARKED SEPARATELY FROM NEW WRITING, because they are
          different work: one is a rewrite against a live URL that already
          ranks, the other is a blank page. -#}
      {%- if entry.migration %}<span class="cs-map-tag">Migration</span>{% endif %}
      {%- if kind %}<span class="cs-map-tag">{{ kind }}</span>{% endif %}
    </p>

    <p class="cs-map-row__meta">
      <span class="cs-map-url">{{ entry.url }}</span>
      <span class="cs-map-kw">{{ entry.keyword }}</span>
    </p>

    {%- if entry.derived %}
    <p class="cs-map-row__counts">
      <span>{{ entry.derived.words }} words</span>
      <span class="{{ "cs-map-flag" if entry.derived.brackets }}">{{ entry.derived.brackets }} bracketed</span>
      <span class="{{ "cs-map-flag" if entry.derived.placeholders }}">{{ entry.derived.placeholders }} placeholder slots</span>
      <span>{{ entry.derived.observed }} observed</span>
      <span>images brief {{ "yes" if entry.derived.images else "no" }}</span>
      <span>blocker note {{ "yes" if entry.derived.blocked else "no" }}</span>
    </p>
    {%- endif %}

    {%- if entry.disagreement %}
    <p class="cs-map-row__flag">Disagreement. {{ entry.disagreement }}</p>
    {%- endif %}

    {%- if entry.blocker %}<p class="cs-map-row__note">Blocker. {{ entry.blocker }}</p>{% endif %}
    {%- if entry.note %}<p class="cs-map-row__note">{{ entry.note }}</p>{% endif %}
  </div>
  {%- endmacro %}

  {#- ---- PILLAR AND PAGE TEMPLATES FIRST, because the clusters hang off them
      and neither is visible in collections.yelp as a plan row. ---- -#}
  <section class="cs-map-section">
    <h2 class="cs-map-h2">Pillar</h2>
    {{ row(report.pillar, "Pillar") }}
  </section>

  <section class="cs-map-section">
    <h2 class="cs-map-h2">Page templates</h2>
    <p class="cs-map-section__note">Not articles. Listed because the clusters hang off them.</p>
    {%- for entry in report.templates %}{{ row(entry) }}{% endfor %}
  </section>

  {#- ---- SEVEN CLUSTERS, IN FILE ORDER. Not sorted: the file's order is the
      coverage map's order, which the comp fixes. ---- -#}
  {%- for cluster in report.clusters %}
  <section class="cs-map-section">
    <h2 class="cs-map-h2" id="{{ cluster.slug }}">{{ cluster.name }}</h2>
    <p class="cs-map-cluster__meta">
      <span>{{ cluster.intent }}</span>
      <span>{{ cluster.spokes.length }} spokes</span>
      <span>{{ cluster.faqCount }} FAQs</span>
      <span class="{{ "cs-map-flag" if not cluster.faqLinkable }}">{{ cluster.faqLinkable }} can link today</span>
    </p>
    {%- if cluster.note %}<p class="cs-map-section__note">{{ cluster.note }}</p>{% endif %}
    {%- for spoke in cluster.spokes %}{{ row(spoke) }}{% endfor %}
  </section>
  {%- endfor %}

  {#- ---- THE WORKLIST. Everything blocking, in one list, ordered by how much
      it can be trusted: measured off a built page, then the file's global
      blockers which carry owners, then per-spoke assertions. ---- -#}
  <section class="cs-map-section cs-map-section--last">
    <h2 class="cs-map-h2">Blockers, all sources</h2>
    <p class="cs-map-section__note">
      Measured first, because those are counted off pages that already exist and
      cannot be out of date. Then the file's global blockers, which carry owners.
      Then per-spoke, every one of which is a plan assertion.
    </p>
    <ol class="cs-map-blockers">
      {%- for blocker in report.blockers %}
      <li>
        <span class="cs-map-kind cs-map-kind--{{ blocker.kind }}">{{ blocker.kind }}</span>
        <span class="cs-map-blockers__what">{{ blocker.what }}</span>
        {%- if blocker.owner %}<span class="cs-map-owner">{{ blocker.owner }}</span>
        {%- else %}<span class="cs-map-owner cs-map-owner--none">unassigned</span>{% endif %}
        <span class="cs-map-blockers__gates">{{ blocker.gates }}</span>
        {%- if blocker.url %}<span class="cs-map-url">{{ blocker.url }}</span>{% endif %}
      </li>
      {%- endfor %}
    </ol>
  </section>

{% endcall %}
